  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U6U-READ-1",
      "title": "Our Graduation Trip",
      "text": "Last summer, our class went to Kenting for a graduation trip. Our teacher asked us to think of a plan by ourselves. Amy found a coupon for a cheap hotel, and I sent a message to confirm the rooms. When we arrived, we had to check in at the front desk, and the clerk had to check up on every name one by one. The hotel did not allow us to cook, so we ate raw fish at a night market instead. The next morning, we surfed at the beach and walked to the peak of a small hill. Nobody discouraged us, even when the rain started. Amy made a short film about the whole trip. Now that film is a reminder of our happiest days together."
    }
  ],
